# SSR

- This is Next.js 16. Read `templates/ssr/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using a Next API. Keep the `nextjs-agent-rules` block in `templates/ssr/AGENTS.md`.
- Server Components are the default. Add `'use client'` only for state, effects, event handlers, or browser APIs. `templates/ssr/src/app/providers.tsx` and the login and tasks pages are client components. The root layout stays a server component.
- Server-only code stays in `templates/ssr/src/server`. Client components talk to route handlers under `templates/ssr/src/app/api` through `getApi()` in `templates/ssr/src/lib/api.ts` with `credentials: 'include'`.
- The session is a `jose` HS256 JWT in the `rl_session` httpOnly cookie (`templates/ssr/src/server/session-token.ts`). `templates/ssr/src/proxy.ts` redirects anonymous users away from `/tasks`. Leave the cookie `httpOnly`, `sameSite: 'lax'`, and `secure` in production.
- Register security headers from `headersFor` in `templates/ssr/next.config.ts`. Production keeps the Content-Security-Policy entry. `poweredByHeader` stays off.
- `SESSION_SECRET` is read only by the server env schema. `REACTLOOM_STRICT_SECRETS=true` must keep refusing the development fallback.
- In this monorepo, `outputFileTracingRoot` points at the workspace root. `create-reactloom` rewrites that to the generated app root. Leave the generated value inside the app.
